# Blind PRE: a sufficient finite-lag window for the supplied two-mark readout

**Status:** independently derived conditional finite-bin estimate, before release of the finite-bin author's candidate. No formal audit or retained-status decision. The exact two-mark effect and prepared-state boundary contrast below are **provisional imported premises**, not independently confirmed here. No other active checker packet, finite-bin author packet, or campaign checkpoint was read.

**Result.** At fixed finite cubic torus, spacing, speed parameter, birth rate, prepared vacuum/one-excitation packet, and first-event interval, the full compensated rotor process has a controlled positive-lag probability. Write \(\tau_*=a/c\). A sufficient choice is

\[
 0<b(g)\le b_*,\qquad \frac{b(g)}{\tau_*g^4}\longrightarrow0.
 \tag{A}
\]

Conditional on the imported boundary contrast, the packet-minus-vacuum probability is

\[
 P_\alpha(g;I,b)-P_0(g;I,b)
 =-2\kappa^2 b g^2 e^{-g^2v_p/2}\,\Xi_I
   +O(\kappa^2 b L_I g^4)
   +O\!\left(\frac{\kappa^2 L_I b^2}{\tau_*g^2}\right),
 \tag{B}
\]

where \(L_I=\int_I e^{-\lambda s}\,ds\) and
\(\Xi_I=\int_I e^{-\lambda s}|\chi_p(s)|^2\,ds\). Thus the coefficient of
\(\kappa^2 b g^2\) tends to \(-2\Xi_I\). For \(\Xi_I>0\), the deficit survives in these finite bins. Condition (A) is sufficient, not an optimality claim. No conclusion about a fixed positive lag as \(g\to0\) follows from this estimate.

The generator during the lag is the original matter-dependent compensated postbirth generator, including all original channel losses. No field-only postbirth evolution, dephasing, or deletion of other possible births is used. A separate labeled microscopic-process comparison, with accuracy resolving \(b g^2\), is required for a microscopic prediction. Its precise content and a finite-register route are given in §7.

